  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Great Apes Conservation Fund</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The purpose of this project is to decrease threats to the Hoolock Gibbon and halt its declining trend in China by working closely with key stakeholders in and around Gaoligongshan National Nature Reserve and Tongbiguan Nature Reserve. This will be done by: 1) evaluating gibbon habitat quality and connectivity in Yingjiang; 2) conducting a socio--economic survey in local communities and soliciting their comments on establishing potential gibbon corridors; 3) holding a stakeholder workshop on enhancing habitat quality and connectivity of gibbons in Yingjiang; 4) delivering training courses to management staff and community rangers on gibbon monitoring and patrolling; 5) establishing and operating a standardized gibbon monitoring and patrolling system; 6) delivering training to local school teachers on knowledge of gibbon conservation and techniques on conservation education; 7) developing local curriculum and a textbook on gibbon conservation; 8) organizing a workshop on how to use the textbook on Hoolock Gibbon conservation; and 9) designing a public awareness poster on the plight and needs of gibbons and distribute it in local communities.</narrative>
  </description>
